ter.v [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.design-under-test.a1], plus deep_counter_props.sv. The top module is deep_counter_formal at the default LIMIT 99 from [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.interface-spec.a1].", "entry": "deep_counter_formal"}, {"path": "deep_counter_props.sv", "kind": "assertions", "title": "Formal wrapper with interface assertions and covers for deep_counter", "summary": "This is the wrapper module deep_counter_formal. It instantiates deep_counter from [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.design-under-test.a1] and states the rules of [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.interface-spec.a1] as port-level properties.\n\nAll assertions are immediate assertions inside always blocks, guarded by if, which is the open front-end subset. There are no assume statements. Range and carry are checked at every step. The covers include the deep wrap scenario and the case where two inputs (clr and en) are high at once.", "entry": "deep_counter_formal"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Expected but not verified: given the DC-RANGE assertion, every property is 1-inductive. From count <= LIMIT, each next count is 0, count+1 with count < LIMIT, or unchanged. So smtbmc induction at depth 110 should close.", "Expected but not verified: every cover and every derived antecedent is reachable within depth 110. The deepest is a wrap after reset, at about step 101.", "Expected but not verified: Yosys read -formal accepts the property file, including $past inside nested if statements in a clocked block.", "Not verified: run time of smtbmc prove at depth 110 on this 7-bit design."], "escalation": null, "notes": "No tool was run by me, so tool_runs is empty. The formal.run and formal.cover evidence must come from the platform's own runs over these files.\n\nThe proof fixes LIMIT at its default of 99, which is the approved instantiation. It does not cover the other values of LIMIT from 1 to 127 named in DC-PARAM. That gap should be stated at review, or covered by further parameterised runs.\n\nI did not write a file name